Here's an example of a banner ad for a toy sale:

```html
<div class="ad-banner" id="ad-slot-300x250" data-ad-id="toy-ads-001" data-campaign="holiday-toys">
 <style>
 .ad-banner { 
 width: 300px; 
 height: 250px; 
 border: 1px solid #ccc; 
 background-color: #f9f9f9; 
 position: relative;
 }
 .ad-banner img { max-width: 100%; }
 .ad-banner .cta-button { 
 position: absolute; 
 bottom: 10px; 
 right: 10px; 
 background-color: #ff9900; 
 color: #fff; 
 padding: 5px 10px; 
 text-decoration: none; 
 border-radius: 3px;
 }
 </style>
 <div class="ad-content">
 <img src="holiday-toys-banner.jpg" alt="Holiday Toy Sale">
 <a href="https://example.com/shop" class="cta-button">Shop Now</a>
 </div>
 <script async src="https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com/pagead/js/adsbygoogle.js"></script>
 <ins class="adsbygoogle"
 style="display:block"
 data-ad-client="ca-pub-123456789"
 data-ad-slot="1234567890"
 data-ad-format="auto"
 data-full-width-responsive="true"></ins>
 <script>
 (adsbygoogle = window.adsbygoogle || []).push({});
 </script>
</div>
```
Classification: is_ad: true
Ad Type: banner

This snippet demonstrates a common ad setup with an image, a "Shop Now" call-to-action button, and integrates Google AdSense for dynamic ad serving. The CSS ensures responsiveness and a user-friendly interface for various screen sizes. Would you like to see an example of non-advertisement content next?

